#: ../../../dev/source_tree_layout.md:3
msgid "LLVM-libc Source Tree Layout"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/source_tree_layout.md:5
msgid ""
"At the top-level, LLVM-libc source tree is organized in to the following "
"directories:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/source_tree_layout.md:25
msgid "Each of these directories is explained briefly below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/source_tree_layout.md:27
msgid "The `benchmarks` directory"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/source_tree_layout.md:29
msgid ""
"The `benchmarks` directory contains LLVM-libc's benchmarking utilities. "
"These are mostly used for the memory functions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/source_tree_layout.md:32
msgid "The `config` directory"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/source_tree_layout.md:34
msgid ""
"The `config` directory contains the default configurations for the targets "
"LLVM-libc supports. These are files in the `config/<platform>/<architecture>/"
"` subdirectory called `entrypoints.txt`, `exclude.txt`, `headers.txt`, and "
"`config.json`. These tell cmake which entrypoints are available, which "
"entrypoints to exclude, which headers to generate, and what options to set "
"for the current target respectively. There are also other platform specific "
"files in the `config/<platform>/` subdirectory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/source_tree_layout.md:42
msgid "The `cmake` directory"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/source_tree_layout.md:44
msgid ""
"The `cmake` directory contains the implementations of LLVM-libc's CMake "
"build rules."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/source_tree_layout.md:47
msgid "The `docs` directory"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/source_tree_layout.md:49
msgid ""
"The `docs` directory contains design docs and also informative documents "
"like this document on source layout."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/source_tree_layout.md:52
msgid "The `fuzzing` directory"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/source_tree_layout.md:54
msgid ""
"This directory contains fuzzing tests for the various components of LLVM-"
"libc. The directory structure within this directory mirrors the directory "
"structure of the top-level `libc` directory itself. For more details, see "
"{doc}`fuzzing`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/source_tree_layout.md:59
msgid "The `hdr` directory"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/source_tree_layout.md:61
msgid ""
"This directory contains proxy headers which are included from the files in "
"the src directory. These proxy headers either include our internal type or "
"macro definitions, or the system's type or macro definitions, depending on "
"if we are in fullbuild or overlay mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/source_tree_layout.md:66
msgid "The `include` directory"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/source_tree_layout.md:68
msgid "The `include` directory contains:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/source_tree_layout.md:70
msgid ""
"`*.h.def` files - These files are used to construct the generated public "
"header files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/source_tree_layout.md:72
msgid ""
"Self contained public header files - These are header files which are "
"already in the form that get installed when LLVM-libc is installed on a "
"user's computer. These are mostly in the `llvm-libc-macros` and `llvm-libc-"
"types` subdirectories."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/source_tree_layout.md:77
msgid "The `lib` directory"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/source_tree_layout.md:79
msgid ""
"This directory contains a `CMakeLists.txt` file listing the targets for the "
"public libraries `libc.a`, `libm.a` etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/source_tree_layout.md:82
msgid "The `src` directory"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/source_tree_layout.md:84
msgid ""
"This directory contains the implementations of the llvm-libc entrypoints. "
"For more details on what an entrypoint is and how it is implemented, see the "
"{ref}`entrypoints` documentation. It is further organized as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/source_tree_layout.md:88
msgid "There is a top-level CMakeLists.txt file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/source_tree_layout.md:89
msgid ""
"For every public header file provided by llvm-libc, there exists a "
"corresponding directory in the `src` directory. The name of the directory is "
"same as the base name of the header file. For example, the directory "
"corresponding to the public `math.h` header file is named `math`. The "
"implementation standard document explains more about the *header* "
"directories."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/source_tree_layout.md:96
msgid "The `startup` directory"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/source_tree_layout.md:98
msgid ""
"This directory contains the implementations of the application startup "
"objects like `crt1.o` etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/source_tree_layout.md:101
msgid "The `test` directory"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/source_tree_layout.md:103
msgid ""
"This directory contains tests for the various components of LLVM-libc. The "
"directory structure within this directory mirrors the directory structure of "
"the toplevel `libc` directory itself. A test for, say the `mmap` function, "
"lives in the directory `test/src/sys/mman/` as implementation of `mmap` "
"lives in `src/sys/mman`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/source_tree_layout.md:109
msgid "The `utils` directory"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/source_tree_layout.md:111
msgid ""
"This directory contains utilities used by other parts of the LLVM-libc "
"system. See the `README` files in the subdirectories within this directory "
"to learn about the various utilities."
msgstr ""
